From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "adnan.drina" <adnan.drina@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:45:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] feat(transport): per-run model request pacer from a
 shared sliding-window ledger

RHOAI3 Stage 080 (architect review R2): the declared request allowance of a
run must be enforced, not only checked. When RHOAI3_REQUEST_BUDGET=<n>/<s>
and RHOAI3_REQUEST_LEDGER=<path> are set, every model HTTP request any
Hermes process of the run sends takes one slot from an append-only,
flock-protected ledger shared by all processes and surviving restarts.
Unset => disabled, behaviour unchanged.

- agent/request_pacer.py: ledger and sliding window, and a PacedAttempt per
  logical request attempt that owns its reservation, its original monotonic
  deadline (created + RHOAI3_REQUEST_BUDGET_MAX_WAIT, default 900 s), its
  cancellation and its waiting status. Every wait made for the attempt
  (reservation, stream reconnect) is charged against that one deadline, so
  a competitor that keeps winning expiring slots cannot extend it; the
  first predicted slot beyond the allowance stops at once. Exhaustion
  raises RequestBudgetExhausted with a named STOP MODEL_REQUEST_BUDGET
  message (worded to avoid the dispatcher's quota/auth respawn-blocker
  pattern) before anything is sent.
- Enforcement: an httpx request event hook attached at the OpenAI client
  construction choke points (agent_runtime_helpers primary client;
  auxiliary_client sync, async and Vertex clients), so each HTTP attempt,
  including every Hermes and SDK retry and stream reconnect, takes exactly
  one slot (POST only).
- Ownership is explicit: the main loop reserves the attempt's slot before
  the API call (outside the stream stale detector) and tags that attempt's
  own request with its id (header X-RHOAI3-Pace-Attempt, removed by the hook
  before sending). Only a request carrying that id consumes the reservation;
  an untagged (auxiliary) request always acquires its own slot with its own
  deadline; a retried attempt is a new attempt. Cancellation is checked
  before a reservation is consumed and before any request is admitted (an
  unused reservation stays counted). The stream attempt binds its own
  cancellation (superseded attempt, interrupt) to the paced attempt.
- The stream stale watchdog exempts only its own attempt's pre-send wait,
  never another thread's pacer wait.
- Exhaustion is never retried and ends the turn with model_stop=
  request_budget, recorded by the shared kanban worker-stop recorder as a
  failed run.
